Why was Java created!?
1991 - Green Project 
James Gosling and a small team at Sun Microsystems explored software for consumer device's 
1991 - Named "Oak"
The new language is named adter an oak tree outside Gosling's office 
1992 - Star7 demo 
A handheld prototype(*7) shows Oak code running on custom hardware 
1995 - Renamed Java 
"Oak" is already trademarked; Java is publicly announced in May 1995
1996 - JDK 1.0
First official release (January 1996)-Java goes mainstream 

How Java evolved: 30 Year's of steady upgrades
Java 1.0 - Jan 1996
JVM,core libraries,applets - Write once,Run anywhere 
Java 5 - Sep 2004
Generics, annotations,enums,enhance for-loops 
Java 8 - Mar 2014
Lambdas,StreamAPI,new date/time API
Java 11 - Sep 2018
First LTS of the 6-month era ; standard HTTP Client 
Java 17 - Sep 2021
Records,sealed classes,text blocks; Spring Boot 3/4 baseline 
Java 21 - Sep 2024
Virtual threads, Pattern matching for switch, record patterns 
Java 25 - Sep 2025
Compact source files,scoped values, compact object headers 

